^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
The variadic arguments start after the last named parameter of the function,
whatever the second argument of va_start is. C23 made that argument optional:
the stdarg.h of GCC 15 and Clang 21 then uses __builtin_c23_va_start, which
CBMC did not know, and those of GCC 13 and 14 and Clang 16 to 20 pass 0, for
which symex failed with "address_arithmetic does not handle constant".
